      "content": "Those cramps are just your body adjusting to the low-carb lifestyle, and they'll pass once you get the hang of it. The lightheadedness is probably due to dehydration, so drink some water and electrolyte-rich beverages like coconut water or bone broth. As for the stomach cramps, I recommend taking some ginger in capsule form or drinking ginger tea to help soothe your digestive system. And to alleviate the cramps, try taking a magnesium supplement, but don't overdo it - just a small dose of 200mg should do the trick.",
